@startuml
left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {
    usecase "View Room\nAvailability" as UC01
    usecase "Book Room" as UC02
    usecase "Cancel Own\nBooking" as UC03
    usecase "Block or Unblock\nRoom" as UC04
    usecase "Review Room\nUsage" as UC05
    usecase "Send Booking\nConfirmation" as UC06
}

Student --> UC01
Student --> UC02
Student --> UC03

Administrator --> UC04
Administrator --> UC05

' why: R4 requires confirmation after every successful booking (US-06).
UC02 ..> UC06 : <<include>>

note right of UC02
R1: Start must be in the future.
Duration > 0 and <= 2 hours.
R2: Active bookings for the
same room cannot overlap.
R3: A blocked room cannot
accept a new booking.
end note

note right of UC06
R4: Every successful booking
produces a confirmation.
end note

note bottom of UC01
Availability reflects:
- existing active bookings (R2)
- blocked rooms (R3)
end note

legend bottom
Assumptions:
1. A Student may cancel only their own booking.
2. "Send Booking Confirmation" occurs only after a successful booking.
3. Booking confirmation is modeled with <<include>> because R4 makes it mandatory.
4. No <<extend>> relationship is used because the approved stories define no optional extension behavior.
5. Cancellation confirmation is excluded from this model.
6. Payments, room equipment, recurring bookings, waiting lists,
   other notifications, and user registration are out of scope.
endlegend

@enduml
